- externalproject-cmp0225-wasm3-libserialport (cmake/deps/BuildWasm3.cmake:15,
  cmake/deps/BuildLibSerialPort.cmake:20): ExternalProject_Add(wasm3_shared, libserialport_static)
  uses the default configure command without CMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX; CMake 4.5 warns (policy CMP0225) on
  every configure. Pass CMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX or set the policy. Found 2026-11-15 on Termux.

- typedarray-prototype-cache-unreferenced: js_typedarray_prototype()
  (src/utils.c:2138) stores the freshly obtained prototype in the static
  `typedarray_prototype` and returns the same value without a
  JS_DupValue(), so the cache holds no reference of its own while the
  caller later frees the one it was handed (js_is_typedarray() does
  `JS_FreeValue(ctx, proto)` right after). Stock QuickJS never notices
  because %TypedArray%.prototype stays alive through Uint8Array's own
  prototype link, but any engine that counts references for real (the
  js-engines N-API adapter, where the box is deleted at count zero) is left
  with a dangling cache: use-after-free and a double free in js_input_chars()
  on the second string argument (Predicate.string('abc')('abc') after any
  earlier call). One-line fix: `typedarray_prototype = JS_DupValue(ctx, ret);`
  before the early `return ret;`. Found while running tests/unittests on
  Bun/Deno/Node through the adapter.

    // bun/deno/node via the adapter:
    //   import { Predicate } from 'predicate';
    //   Predicate.charset('abc')('b'); Predicate.string('abc')('abc');
    //   -> free(): double free detected in tcache 2
